  "FP_PIN_ORDER_CFG": "dir::pin_order.cfg",
  "_comment_pinorder": "FP_PIN_ORDER_CFG (pin_order.cfg) places CPU-side pins (ibus_*/a_mmu_*/ctrl_*/lock) on the EAST edge and memory-side pins (dbus_*/snpc_*) on the WEST edge so an integrating top can abut this macro's CPU port to the CPU and its memory port to the DDR/flash side with minimal top-level routing. PL_TARGET_DENSITY_PCT kept at 30 (pin-order adds edge placement pressure; the CTS clock tree needs spread room in the macro-bound margins).",
  "_comment_flat": "dcache SOUTH of CPU: CPU pins+tags NORTH, memory EAST. 4 tags contiguous top-center (cols 2-5), the center slot below them (col3 row1) left open as a routing pocket, 16 data around. Tightened col gaps (inner 90) + row gap (60). Col x=[50, 552, 1074, 1596, 2117, 2639, 3141], bbox 3573x1625. Die 3700x1750 -> 3620x1700."
